Human intervention needed

The automated job failed in `explore/generate_tests()` while generating reporter-requested metadata for `io.netty:netty-handler-proxy:4.2.1.Final`.

Preserved work: https://github.com/oracle/graalvm-reachability-metadata/tree/ai%2Fkimeta%2Fhuman-intervention%2Fissue-9341-fails-native-image-run-io.netty-netty-handler-proxy-4.2.1.Final-aa82a860

Evidence:
- The continuation marker records `explore/generate_tests()` as the failure location, and metrics report failure after 3 iterations with 0 generated LOC and identical starting/ending commit `def241db853`.
- Native tests initially failed 9/10 times with an NPE at `PlatformDependent0.safeConstructPutInt` through Netty 4.2.1’s `AdaptivePoolingAllocator`.
- An `UnpooledByteBufAllocator` workaround made all 10 native tests pass, but the trace-enabled binary then failed during JUnit discovery with `StackOverflowError`.
